+subdir: hermes-plugin
+title: "Hermes in the Browser"
+description: "Settings page (in the language set in Hermes, nine languages; incl. which browser Hermes works in and its safety level; loosening must be confirmed in the browser) and guard rails for hermes-tabs, which lets Hermes work in individual tabs of your real, signed-in Chromium browser through an extension and an MCP relay. Disclosure — talks only to the hermes-tabs relay you configure (HERMES_TABS_RELAY, default 127.0.0.1:8766) with HERMES_TABS_ADMIN_TOKEN (paths /admin/settings and /admin/select, the latter picks the browser when several are connected); caches the last seen settings in plugin-data/hermes-tabs/settings.json and its own opt-in switch in plugin-data/hermes-tabs/options.json; the pre_tool_call hook rejects the tabs tools while switched off and, only if the user turns that switch on, blocked sites in Hermes' own browser tools and web_extract. No shell, no background processes, no telemetry."
