ueries that hold one, are not sent; a failure or a slow answer gives the recall of rerank: off and pauses the endpoint (60 s, doubling to 900 s); nothing the endpoint returns is stored; the bundled language dictionaries are gzip-compressed plain-text word lists; with auto_extract on (off by default) user sentences that state a preference or decision are stored. Since 0.19.0, fact_store merge combines duplicate facts in one transaction while keeping each copy's history, sources and confirmations under its original id. The retained fact keeps its own text, trust and origin; copies leave current search and recall. Optional expect pins the exact shown versions and refuses changed participants without a write. Scheduled jobs can merge only copies created in their own session. Forgetting the retained fact also erases its merged copies. Merge is local and makes no new network or model calls. Version 0.19.1 adds strict tooling for comparing recorded margins; the normal RECALL_MARGIN remains 1.0. Version 0.19.2 closes a timed-out rerank or embeddings request socket so a server dripping response headers does not keep its worker alive. During TLS wrapping, cancellation is retained but the handshake can continue until its own socket timeout; DNS resolution is outside socket cancellation. Version 0.20.0 adds an opt-in local task-outcome journal and the memory-provider tool fact_experience: emitted and candidate fact/version identifiers, an optional short task and correction, outcome/reason and optional corrected-source references. It is separate from trust, origin and ranking. Agent reports are not authenticated human confirmations. Collection and detailed tracing are off by default; retention is bounded to 30 days and 1000 attempts per store, with up to 10 revisions per attempt. Forgetting any referenced fact removes the dependent attempt and outcome from the store. No new model, network or credential use; synchronous local writes add latency. PR #45 also loads NumPy on first use outside the plugin-loader lock; concurrent first callers wait for import completion. Version 0.20.1 limits SQLite busy waits for the optional journal and retries transient contention once. Failed receipts are reported and are not queued; the SQLite timeout is not a full search deadline. Version 0.20.2 writes no receipt for a prefetch that emits nothing, applies journal retention whenever a writer opens the store (also with the journal off) and scrubs removed outcome text from the file like a forgotten fact. Version 0.20.3 adds one system-prompt line, only with the journal on, asking the agent to record an outcome when the person corrects an answer that used recalled facts (an agent report, not human confirmation). Version 0.21.0 adds an opt-in prefetch_max_tokens budget for the recalled block: facts that do not fit are left out whole, never cut; off by default. Version 0.22.0 keeps entity links honest on a text change: a new entities list replaces the declared names, and a declared name the new text no longer says is dropped; revert restores a version's declared names from an additive version_names table (names with keyed hashes, removed with the version and by delete_entity in every spelling a tombstone covers, including by older releases through triggers). Version 0.22.1 makes the secret/instruction screen about 30× faster on long texts with the same decisions (patterns unchanged; a prefilter chooses where they are tried). Version 0.22.2 sends a slow reranker only as many of the first candidates as its measured speed answers in half rerank_timeout (at least two), so a large pool no longer times out and pauses the endpoint; the candidates not sent keep their order behind the scored ones. Version 0.23.0 stops feedback (helpful/unhelpful) from refreshing a fact's age: optional temporal decay counts from when the current version was recorded, and updated_at changes only when the fact itself does; a correction with a new text (correct / update content) starts at its origin's trust without the old text's helpful marks, recalls and confirmations, like change, while a date-only correction keeps them and revert restores the old trust. Version 0.23.1 takes a correction that journal retention removed off the disk on the open connection (the file rewrite runs after the receipt write, with busy timeout 0 at every step) and clears only the rewrite mark it served. Version 0.24.0 adds two experimental features, both off by default and with no new network, model or credential use: memory_map.py, a command-line exporter nothing in the provider calls, which prints one store as a read-only JSON snapshot for a person to read (opened mode=ro in one read transaction; a forgotten fact is its id and date only; corrected versions and texts the safety screen hides carry no text; with --config it reads config.yaml's search settings, with --hermes-home the hermes-dreaming files about the profile store), whose output holds the facts' texts and so is personal data; and prefetch_clause_coverage: on, which gives each of two separate Russian or English questions in one message a second look at the facts the coverage gate left out. Version 0.25.0 limits the memory map export to 1000 facts and 300 names by default (--max-facts / --max-entities, 0 for none) and says what it cut in SNAP.limits; nothing else changes. Version 0.25.1 fixes recall by meaning dropping a fact that names a short Russian name in another grammatical case than the message (Eva as «Ева» / «Еву»): the name now also meets a capitalized word of the fact that may be a case form of it. Version 0.25.2 reads that word by its case ending rather than a short stem: names whose stem changes meet their forms («Лев» / «Льва»), and different names that only shared a short stem («Аня» / «Анна») no longer meet; nothing else changes. Version 0.25.3 no longer imports NumPy when the provider starts (the first search that needs it does, as does opening a store whose vectors need re-encoding) and treats a NumPy that is installed but fails to import as missing, so recall goes on by words; finds a Latin word written into Chinese, Japanese, Korean or Thai text by itself; refuses at write, and leaves out of recall, a prompt addressed to an assistant and the agent's report of its own steps; and auto_extract (off by default) no longer stores a reply such as \"I like that\" as a preference; no change to defaults, schema or network behaviour. Version 0.26.0 adds an experimental presence gate, prefetch_presence_gate (off by default): with it on, a fact this provider injected is held back past the six-turn repeat window only while the model can verifiably still see it (its exact recall line inside a <memory-context> block the core fenced, or its fact id and text in a fact_store result), reading only the messages the core already passes to sync_turn, with no new storage, network, model or credential use; tool results now carry raw Unicode instead of Unicode escape sequences (a payload that cannot be encoded keeps the escaped form); change names the keywords it drops and correct writes the keywords it is given; with the gate off, recall is unchanged. Version 0.26.1 fixes that gate after an independent review: a sync the core queued before a compaction no longer counts as the current view, a fact the compaction removed is recalled again once a fresh view no longer shows it, a compaction that fails no longer switches the gate off for the session, a late sync keeps its own turn, and a fact_store history result counts as the fact being visible; with the gate off nothing changes. Version 0.26.2: with the task-outcome journal on (off by default), a prefetch that only refreshes facts the session already holds records no new attempt and carries no Memory attempt line, so a repeated block adds nothing new to the context."
