+name: mqtt
+repo: https://github.com/JasonSwindle/hermes-mqtt
+sha: 103ec28e9e2f68b080fd8e8074d0e5a98750e06e
+description: "MQTT as a Hermes platform: one authenticated broker connection, per-topic routing (deliver, agent, job, drop) and JSON replies published outside the consumed namespace; ships its own standard-library MQTT 3.1.1/5.0 client over TCP or TLS (verified by default, optional private CA/mTLS) with keepalive, reconnect and opt-in burst coalescing, and drops unmatched topics. Disclosure — holds one outbound broker connection and its reconnect loop, reads the MQTT username/password through Hermes's scoped secret route and optional TLS files at operator-provided paths, and enables trusted_inbound (the broker's authentication is the trust boundary): any publisher the broker's ACL admits can start agent turns, and on topics you map to deliver or job it can post text to the chat you name on another connected platform or run the cron job you name, while payload text can never issue gateway commands; job and cross-platform delivery go through Hermes internals (tools.cronjob_tools, the gateway runner), so a Hermes update can disable them; no telemetry, no shell, no writes."
+maintainer: JasonSwindle
+tier: community
+category: platform
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22.3,<0.23"
+docs_url: https://github.com/JasonSwindle/hermes-mqtt#readme
